{# =====================================================================
   Template: node_draft_prose  (Module M06 — Drafting & Generation)
   Rendered by prompts/prompt_loader.py (StrictUndefined, autoescape=False).

   Unlike the planner templates, this is NOT a deliberation loop — it is a
   single-shot generation prompt. The model streams free-text prose; the
   harness never asks it for JSON, an action, or a self-check here.

   Expected context variables (ALL required — StrictUndefined; omitting any
   raises). node_draft_prose supplies every variable from the assembled
   active_context_package plus the active beat plan produced by the planning
   cascade.

   Context-package layers (node_assemble_context; epistemic status labelled):
     relational_facts    : dict  — canonical SQLite facts around the active
                                    pointer, ABSOLUTE TRUTH; includes confirmed
                                    coreference facts under its own key.
     epistemic_beliefs    : list — unconfirmed coreference candidates, each
                                    EXPLICITLY FLAGGED as an assumption, not a
                                    settled fact; may be empty.
     summary_context      : dict — RAPTOR summary-tree context; lower
                                    authority than relational_facts.
     flavour_passages     : list — optional colour/associative passages;
                                    lowest authority; may be empty.
     temporal_context     : dict — temporal/graph context; may be empty while
                                    that store is stubbed.
     macro_constraints    : dict — approved macro constraints + compiled
                                    annotations for the ACTIVE CHAPTER (only
                                    present in macro mode); may be an empty
                                    dict when no macro layer applies — the
                                    section below still renders cleanly.

   Active beat plan (from the planning cascade, computed — never invented
   here):
     beat_immediate_objective   : str  — the ONE concrete thing this beat
                                    accomplishes on the page.
     beat_physical_constraints  : list — concrete staging/blocking facts the
                                    prose must obey (who is where, what they
                                    hold, distances, light, exits, injuries).
     active_continuity          : dict — the beat's entry_condition,
                                    exit_condition, and any continuity_facts
                                    it must respect; the prose must land in
                                    the exit_condition's state, not before it
                                    and not past it.
     pad_behavioral_constraint  : str  — the grounded behavioural-constraint
                                    string for this beat's affect target,
                                    COMPUTED BY THE PLANNING PIPELINE. Write
                                    prose consistent with this register — do
                                    NOT restate, adjust, or compute affect
                                    values; that is not this model's job.

   Continuation & sizing (supplied by the node, never hardcoded here):
     prior_prose_tail     : str  — the tail of the preceding committed prose;
                                    empty string when this is the scene's
                                    first beat.
     scene_entry_state    : str  — the scene's entry state, so the draft has
                                    a concrete starting point even with no
                                    prior prose.
     target_word_count    : int  — target word-count guidance for this beat.
   ===================================================================== #}
<drafting_task>

  <role>
    You are the Drafter for a long-form novel. You turn an assembled context
    package and one approved beat plan into the beat's prose — nothing else.
    You do not plan, you do not audit, and you do not decide what happens
    next; the beat plan below already fixes the objective, staging, and
    affect. Your only job is to write the beat so it lands exactly where the
    plan says it must land.
  </role>

  <drafting_objective>
    Write the prose for the CURRENT beat only. The prose must:
      - accomplish the beat's immediate_objective and nothing more — a beat
        with two objectives is two beats; stop once this one is done.
      - obey every physical_constraint below as hard staging — do not move a
        character, object, or condition the constraints have not authorized.
      - begin from the beat's entry state (the prior prose's tail, or the
        scene's entry state if there is none) and end at its exit_condition —
        no earlier, no later.
      - read consistent with the affect_target's behavioral_constraint below:
        write a character who would plausibly behave this way, without ever
        naming, restating, or computing the underlying affect values.
      - respect canonical relational facts as absolute truth, treat flagged
        Epistemic Beliefs as unconfirmed (never state one as settled fact),
        and use summary and flavour context only as background colour, never
        as a source that can override canonical facts or the beat plan.
      - honor every hard requirement below over any soft preference; if the
        macro layer supplies approved constraints or compiled annotations for
        this chapter, the prose must not contradict them.
    Output prose only: no outline, no meta-commentary, no headings, no
    summary of what you wrote, no author's notes.
  </drafting_objective>

  <context>
    <canonical_relational_facts note="Absolute truth for this beat, including confirmed coreference facts. Never contradict these.">{{ relational_facts | tojson | xmlsafe }}</canonical_relational_facts>
    <epistemic_beliefs note="UNCONFIRMED coreference candidates — write around these as open possibilities, never as settled fact.">
    {% for belief in epistemic_beliefs %}
      - [UNCONFIRMED ASSUMPTION] {{ belief | tojson | xmlsafe }}
    {% else %}
      (none flagged for this beat)
    {% endfor %}
    </epistemic_beliefs>
    <summary_context note="RAPTOR summary-tree background — lower authority than canonical facts.">{{ summary_context | tojson | xmlsafe }}</summary_context>
    <flavour_passages note="Optional colour only — lowest authority; never overrides canonical facts or the beat plan.">
    {% for passage in flavour_passages %}
      - {{ passage | tojson | xmlsafe }}
    {% else %}
      (none available for this beat)
    {% endfor %}
    </flavour_passages>
    <temporal_context note="Temporal/graph background for this beat.">{{ temporal_context | tojson | xmlsafe }}</temporal_context>
  </context>

  <macro_constraints note="Approved macro constraints and compiled annotations for the active chapter. Hard constraints override preferences and must not be contradicted.">
  {% if macro_constraints %}
    <hard_requirements>
    {% for c in macro_constraints.get('hard_annotations', []) %}
      - {{ c.get('text', c) | xmlsafe }}
    {% else %}
      (none)
    {% endfor %}
    </hard_requirements>
    <preferences>
    {% for c in macro_constraints.get('soft_preferences', []) %}
      - {{ c.get('text', c) | xmlsafe }}
    {% else %}
      (none)
    {% endfor %}
    </preferences>
  {% else %}
    (no macro constraints for this pass — proceed on the beat plan and continuity context alone)
  {% endif %}
  </macro_constraints>

  <beat_plan note="Computed by the planning cascade — write to satisfy this exactly; never revise it.">
    <immediate_objective>{{ beat_immediate_objective | xmlsafe }}</immediate_objective>
    <physical_constraints>
    {% for constraint in beat_physical_constraints %}
      - {{ constraint | xmlsafe }}
    {% else %}
      (none recorded — treat the scene's entry state below as the only staging authority)
    {% endfor %}
    </physical_constraints>
    <active_continuity note="The state this beat starts from and the state it must end in.">{{ active_continuity | tojson | xmlsafe }}</active_continuity>
  </beat_plan>

  <affect_target note="COMPUTED BY THE PLANNING PIPELINE — write consistent with this register. Do NOT name, restate, or compute affect values in the prose.">
    <behavioral_constraint>{{ pad_behavioral_constraint | xmlsafe }}</behavioral_constraint>
  </affect_target>

  <continuation>
    <prior_prose_tail note="The tail of the preceding committed prose — continue seamlessly from here.">
    {% if prior_prose_tail %}{{ prior_prose_tail | xmlsafe }}{% else %}(none — this is the scene's first beat; begin from the scene entry state below){% endif %}
    </prior_prose_tail>
    <scene_entry_state>{{ scene_entry_state | xmlsafe }}</scene_entry_state>
  </continuation>

  <generation_parameters>
    <target_word_count>{{ target_word_count }}</target_word_count>
  </generation_parameters>

  <output_contract>
    Write the beat's prose now. Output prose text ONLY: no JSON, no markdown
    fence, no headings, no outline, no meta-commentary, no restatement of the
    beat plan, and no author's notes before or after the prose. Aim for the
    target word count above as guidance, not a hard cutoff — end the beat
    when its exit_condition is reached, not before and not after.
  </output_contract>

</drafting_task>
